// Backlog B04: shaking the helicopter in a tunnel. Midday in Port Vesper v2, a racer already at
// wanted level L3 (heat 50, the bottom of L3) follows the route from the Lantern Run grid
// through downtown and Mercer, up the Uptown Connector and into Founders Cut (the 250 m covered
// trench), and stops at the "Founders Cut lay-by" in the middle of it. The route driver seeks
// the lay-by with wp_world's path follower (speed planned for the curves and junctions), so a
// change in junction geometry shifts the timing a little but not the story. A downtown patrol
// starts the pursuit within seconds; the helicopter launches at ≈ 58 s and sits over the racer
// from ≈ 65 s while the ground units fall 300-500 m behind. Inside the Cut nothing outside can
// see in: the helicopter loses the racer as it enters (≈ 100 s) and the L3 day escape time
// (22 s) runs out at ≈ 122 s → Escaped, while the nearest ground unit is still ≈ 400 m away
// (a unit that later drives into the Cut sees him inside the same tunnel).
//
// Heat 50 rather than 55: pursuit heat (0.25/s while seen) took a heat-55 racer to L4 (30 s
// escape time) just before the Cut, and after the round-12b junction fix (≈ 3 s later arrival)
// the first unit drove into the Cut 0.5 s before that timer ran out — a race this scenario
// should not depend on.
//
// The same run with `covered_los: false` (tunnel_escape_founders_cut_control.ron) is captured
// instead: the helicopter keeps watching the parked car until ground units arrive.
//
// Round 13 (rows 63 / 64, faster police that converge and search): pursuit heat now takes him
// to L4 (30 s escape time) at ≈ 97 s, just before the Cut, and searching units used to drive
// into the Cut and find him at ≈ 127 s (captured 138.6 s). Searching units now hold the portal
// nearer to them when the racer is lost inside a covered road (PVPD doctrine §5: nobody chases
// inside), so he escapes after 30 s unseen with the nearest unit ≈ 130 m away at a portal.
// Measured (round 13, racer target 25 m/s): lost at ≈ 101 s, Escaped 131.2 s; control Captured
// 129.3 s, never unseen long. Re-aim with `examples/probe_tunnel_chase.rs`.
//
// After the lead/round12 car-data retune (stiffer dampers on every car, 2026-10-20) the units
// catch him on the Uptown Connector (PIT at ≈ 71 s), which takes him to L5 (40 s escape time) at
// ≈ 77 s. He still reaches the Cut first and is lost inside at ≈ 112.5 s with the units holding
// the portals (nearest ≈ 135 m), so the escape lands at ≈ 152.5 s: the run is 170 s long and the
// escape window ends at 170 s.
//
// Row 119 (solid terrain = drawn terrain): seed 51 hinged on pool unit 11 snagging on invisible
// terrain behind a lot at (-836, 306); on the drawn ground it is stuck a second later, and the
// chase flips to a PIT capture at 70.4 s. Seeds 52-57 are bit-identical with and without that
// fix, and only seed 56 tells this story there (as only 51 and 56 did before): helicopter at
// 63.6 s, lost inside the Cut at ≈ 96 s, Escaped at 118.4 s (L3). Re-seeded to 56.
// Round 12c (rows 80 / 89, police see 380 m by day, 200° forward plus 60 m all round): seed 56
// is now PIT-captured at 54.3 s on the way downtown, before the Cut. Over seeds 50-63 the story
// holds on 8 of 14 seeds (seeds 50, 51, 53, 58-61, 63 escape in the Cut at L3); re-seeded to 51:
// Escaped 118.4 s, max time unseen 21.9 s; control captured 112.1 s.
// Row 84 (search extras, 2026-10-22): extra units sent to the last known spot shift this chase's
// timeline (seed 51 lost him on Mercer at 64.5 s and he escaped at 80.4 s, before the helicopter).
// Seeds 50-63: the escape story holds on 12 of 14, escape and control both on 7 (53-55, 57, 59,
// 60, 62); re-seeded to 53.
// World merge 6799200b (D's Loop 9 rest stops add off/on ramps and parking roads to Port Vesper):
// the new roads change the seeded police spawn spots, and seed 53 diverged at 17.6 s; no unit
// was near Mercer to re-acquire him at ~72 s, so he escaped at 80.4 s before the helicopter.
// Seeds 50-63 on the merged tip: escape story on 11 of 14, both scenarios on 4 (54-56, 58); 54
// and 55 held both before the merge too. Re-seeded to 54.
// Row 156 (owner decision, 2026-10-23: helicopter from wanted level 5, spikes from 4): from heat
// 50 (L3) the run never reached L5 and the helicopter never launched. Heat 90 (the bottom of L5)
// keeps the story: pursuit at 9.8 s, helicopter at 72.2 s, lost inside the Cut, Escaped at
// 133.8 s after 40 s unseen (the L5 day escape time); control Captured at 125.8 s.
// Row 157 (2026-10-23: every heat gain halved): from heat 90 the racer drops below L5 and climbs
// back at half the rate, so the helicopter launched at 95.7-111.2 s on every seed 50-63 (deadline
// 95 s). Heat 95 -> seeds 50-63: escape story on 8 of 14 (51-53, 55-57, 63), control captured in
// its window on 2 (54, 63; the other 12 are still in pursuit at 190 s or captured early, none
// escapes). Re-seeded 54 -> 63, heat 90 -> 95.
// PR #60 port (2026-10-23: no AI pursuit cap, stronger police cars, rolling-block deadlock fix):
// seed 63 was Captured at 141.8 s. Seeds 50-70 at heat 95: escape story on 16 of 21, control
// on 20, both on 15 (50-52, 56-62, 64-66, 68-70). Re-seeded 63 -> 60, the middle of 56-62.
// Row 168 (2026-10-24: a unit in a stopped racer's lane drives on, units wedged against a wall
// or in the racer's lane ahead don't make the arrest): seed 60 was Captured at 132.7 s. Seeds
// 50-70: escape story on 11 of 21, control on 20, both on 11 (50, 52, 54, 56-59, 61, 63, 65,
// 68). Re-seeded 60 -> 58.
// PR #64 (owner 2026-10-23, Core day patrols 8 -> 3, investigations less sensitive) re-seeded
// 54 -> 56 on its own base; on main the seed is re-measured in the police PR port.
// Police PR port (2026-10-24): PR #66 (commit 4b683c3d) turned the AI captain's own tools off
// here (`police_tools: false`): after its road-centre fix the captain lays spikes on the
// straight before the first bend and the flat tyres stop the racer at ~80-90 % of the route.
// This scenario is about covered-road line of sight, not tools. The switch was lost in the
// PR's later merge of main; restored. Seed 58 was then Captured at 110.9 s. Seeds 50-70: both
// files pass on 10 of 21 (51-54, 56, 57, 60, 62, 63, 66); 51-54 is the widest run. Re-seeded
// 58 -> 52.
(
    name: "police_tunnel_escape_founders_cut",
    // Lead 2026-10-24: re-seeded 60 -> 58 after merging D's canal-bridge fix (ws/world 3affce58) with the PR #60 police power port; seed 60's main run became a capture. Seeds 50-70: both files pass on 11 of 21; 56-59 is the widest run, 58 its middle.
    seed: 52,
    city: preset(name: "vesper_v2", seed: 1),
    time_of_day_h: 12.0,
    time_ratio: 1.0,
    mode: Simulation,
    traffic_density: 0.0,
    parked_cars: false,
    police_presence: 1.0,
    police_tools: false,
    assists: ai,
    slow: true,
    entities: [
        (
            id: "racer",
            car: "debug_coupe",
            police_heat: 95.0,
            speed_mps: 20.0,
            driver: follow_route(route_id: "Lantern Run -> Founders Cut lay-by", target_speed: 25.0),
        ),
    ],
    duration_s: 170.0,
    hash_every: 240,
    expect: [
        pursuit_started_before(t_s: 15.0),
        // wp_police HeloLaunched (kind 12). Turn-round round (crawl 4 -> 5.5 m/s, 2026-10-22): the
        // helicopter launches at 90.2 s (was < 80), still before he reaches the Cut.
        police_event_before(kind: 12, t_s: 95.0),
        metric(entity: "racer", name: "route_progress", min: 0.97, max: 1.0),
        // The tunnel hides him long enough for the escape timer (22 s at L3 by day).
        metric(entity: "racer", name: "max_los_lost_s", min: 18.0, max: 60.0),
        first_pursuit_end(entity: "racer", outcome: "Escaped", min_s: 105.0, max_s: 170.0),
        total_loss(entity: "racer", expected: false),
    ],
)
